attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a long spine.** Columns 0 to 12, `periplasmic protein` to `iclR`, are carried by 97 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 42% of calls {S1}. The model names 89 to 99.6% of them, fewest at column 7, `yjbD`, 89% {S1}.

@variable **A single fork column breaks the first spine**: column 13, carried by 42%, all shell, the most plastic stretch of the window {S2, P}. Then the `ace` genes, columns 14 to 16, [[isocitrate]] {S3, Q}. Further along, columns 68 to 71, `frwB` to `fsa`, are [[fructose transport]] {S10, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 97 against 93%, and hesitates less there, 0.15 against 0.22 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 13, is a fork column, at 0.66 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on fork and variable columns.** Columns 66 to 79, `pflC` to `metB`, are carried by 47 to 88% of chromosomes, 13 persistent and 1 shell {S10}. The last column is `metB`, in 47% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 96% of genes**, 0.17 bits on average, perplexity 1.2 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.46 against 0.15 bits, and names fewer genes, 88% against 96% {C}.

